   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "TWELVE JAPANESE BYTES · MiniMax H3 on a 12 GB card · Beyond the Frame\n\nRe-select your own model, encoder and VAE files in the loaders. Red = a teaching from the video.\n\n壱 SQUEEZE THE STEEL — 8-bit model (pruned INT8) + 4-bit text encoder (NVFP4).\n   https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3\n\n参 THE ATTENDANT (offloading) — ComfyUI moves weights to system RAM on its own.\n   Small card: start ComfyUI with  --lowvram  and have plenty of system RAM.\n   OOM with memory to spare?  --disable-dynamic-vram\n\n伍 CLEAR THE FLOOR — VRAM-Cleanup unloads every model, then the plain VAE Decode gets the whole card.\n   Install: ComfyUI Manager → 'Comfyui-Memory_Cleanup' (LAOGOU-666). Update ComfyUI: the H3 decode got ~2× faster.\n\nFrames must fit n % 17 == 5: 124 (~5 s), 209 (~8.7 s), 243 (~10 s).\n\n六 PIKA H3 FLEX — official Comfy settings: ONE adapter at strength 1.0, lcm sampler,\n   ManualSigmas 1.0, 0.972973, 0.923077, 0.8, 0.571429, 0.333333, 0.0, CFG 1 (BasicGuider).\n   Don't stack a turbo / Lightning LoRA on top, don't change the sigmas or the strength.\n   Adapter → models/loras: pika_h3_flex_fl2va_v1_bf16.safetensors\n   https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/blob/main/loras/pika_h3_flex_fl2va_v1_bf16.safetensors\n   Reference-to-video: use pika_h3_flex_ref2va_v1_bf16 + the ref2va base model instead.\n\n   Need the low_vram switch? Use TJB_4b_Pika_H3_Flex_low_vram.json."
   ]
  }
